      "sourceTextSha256": "99bee7f0f3dd4592ed4c42582c2618374cacb4dbb2b5ce2871fb236921532a8a",
      "text": "Breakfast, then transfer to the airport for your flight to Lima.\n\nWe’ll meet you at Lima airport for the drive to Paracas, which takes around **4 hours**.\n\nSpend two nights at **Paracas, a Luxury Collection Resort**, in a **Deluxe Garden View** room. The rest of your time is free.\n\nThe Paracas Peninsula is a national reserve protected for its natural richness and archaeological significance. This vast desert area stretches along the Pacific coast. The reserve is listed as a UNESCO Natural World Heritage Site.\n\nThe landscape here is unlike what you might expect from a national park. The area was once covered by the ocean, so the soil is highly saline and supports very little vegetation. A crust of salt covers the terracotta and burgundy sand, and gently rolling dunes give the landscape an almost otherworldly appearance.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kyprr-kcrymv07az",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
    },
